# the whole reply arrived as one RFCOMM chunk of 39 bytes, 47.2 ms after the write; the
#   connect before it took 122 ms, with the main thread turning the main run loop
# this is the capture that disproved the reversed start-of-packet. On the wire the host
#   word is 08 ee and the device's is 09 ff, not ee 08 and ff 09: Gadgetbridge's
#   (short)0xee08 and (short)0xff09 are written through a little-endian ByteBuffer, so
#   those constants are not the wire order, and reading them as such was the mistake
# the write is command 0x0101 with no payload, a pure read; the reply decodes as volume
#   25, battery 4 fifths = 80 %, not charging, not playing, voice prompts off, auto
#   power-off on with duration index 2, firmware 3.0.4, serial ACCLXX0000000000x
